WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:11.532
Josh and Anne are gearing up for another adventure in the great outdoors.

2
00:00:12.232 --> 00:00:17.556
For this trip, they will spend two weeks backpacking through New Zealand, which sounds like fun, don't you

3
00:00:17.596 --> 00:00:23.260
think? However, this adventure will require getting some special gear before they head out.

4
00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:29.364
Anne and Josh decide to visit a store that sells a lot of backpacking supplies.

5
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.082
Anne knows that the most important piece of equipment for when she's about to do a lot of

6
00:00:34.142 --> 00:00:35.964
hiking, is strong boots.

7
00:00:36.764 --> 00:00:42.647
She tries out a number of boots, walking up and down plastic mountains in the store to test

8
00:00:42.707 --> 00:00:44.148
how well they hold the ground.

9
00:00:45.569 --> 00:00:52.433
It looks like she has found some boots that are very light, waterproof, strong, and her favorite color─yellow!

10
00:00:53.074 --> 00:00:56.936
Josh, meanwhile, knows that the next most important purchase is poles.

11
00:00:57.564 --> 00:01:03.167
Scientists have recently discovered that walking downhill with a lot of weight is difficult for the knees to

12
00:01:03.207 --> 00:01:10.811
handle. In fact, a lot of people injure their knees by slipping downhill, but poles help the knees

13
00:01:10.891 --> 00:01:13.052
by providing extra support and balance.

14
00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:18.896
So Josh chooses some poles that are lightweight but strong enough to support his weight and grip the

15
00:01:18.936 --> 00:01:23.038
ground. The last big purchase is a backpack.

16
00:01:23.638 --> 00:01:26.920
Backpacks come in all colors, sizes, and weights.

17
00:01:27.792 --> 00:01:33.015
Bags that hold over seven kilograms have a padded strap that goes around the waist to help lift

18
00:01:33.055 --> 00:01:34.236
the weight off the shoulders.

19
00:01:35.176 --> 00:01:40.700
Josh picks a brown pack that will help him hide in the trees, and Anne picks a pack

20
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.861
with her favorite color─yellow!

21
00:01:43.881 --> 00:01:47.664
There are a lot more pieces of equipment that Josh and Anne will need to go on their

22
00:01:47.704 --> 00:01:56.052
trip, such as headlamps, sleeping bags, a cookstove, food, hiking clothes, a first aid kit, and bug repellant.

23
00:01:56.072 --> 00:02:00.756
However, all of this can get expensive, so they borrow a lot of these things from their friends.

24
00:02:00.776 --> 00:02:07.401
"In order to stay safe when you go backpacking, it's important to have good gear," Josh says.

25
00:02:08.222 --> 00:02:11.104
Their bags are packed, and they are on their way to New Zealand!

26
00:02:11.765 --> 00:02:15.048
New Zealand is a beautiful country with many kinds of landscapes.

27
00:02:15.888 --> 00:02:21.093
There are beaches, forests, jungles, plains, mountains, and volcanoes, just to name a few.

28
00:02:22.894 --> 00:02:26.841
The country is about the same size as Korea, just a tiny bit bigger.

29
00:02:27.422 --> 00:02:31.785
But there are seventy million people living in Korea and only four million living in New Zealand.

30
00:02:32.425 --> 00:02:37.028
Of course, you can change the total to four million and two, now that Josh and Anne have

31
00:02:37.068 --> 00:02:42.232
landed! There are countless trails and hikes to choose from when you visit this beautiful country.

32
00:02:44.053 --> 00:02:49.317
Josh and Anne decide to try the most famous trail in New Zealand, which is nicknamed the Most

33
00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:50.658
Beautiful Walk in the World.

34
00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:53.280
It is a trail called the Milford Track.

35
00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.782
It will take four days to hike the 53 kilometers from one side of the mountain to the

36
00:02:57.862 --> 00:03:03.764
other. And because so many people like to visit Milford, they will sleep in huts instead of tents

37
00:03:04.064 --> 00:03:05.725
because it is easier on the wildlife.

38
00:03:06.465 --> 00:03:09.026
Josh and Anne arrive at Milford on a very sunny day.

39
00:03:10.026 --> 00:03:14.908
After walking a few kilometers, they pass by a river that is a color of blue Anne has

40
00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:16.449
never seen in a river before.

41
00:03:17.189 --> 00:03:20.030
She is tempted to dive in, but it is too cold!

42
00:03:21.651 --> 00:03:24.492
Later on in the hike, Josh meets a kea.

43
00:03:24.512 --> 00:03:27.774
Don't be fooled, this is a very smart and talented bird.

44
00:03:28.554 --> 00:03:32.476
While people aren't looking, it will unzip their backpacks and steal their lunches.

45
00:03:33.297 --> 00:03:38.280
Josh gets close enough to take a picture and leaves the disappointed kea waiting for its next victim.

46
00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.962
At the top of the mountain is Mackinnon Pass.

47
00:03:42.482 --> 00:03:45.303
The view is breathtaking, and so is the freezing wind!

48
00:03:45.964 --> 00:03:50.186
As they walk down the other side of the mountain, Josh and Anne are glad they have their

49
00:03:50.226 --> 00:03:53.628
poles. Along the way they find a powerful waterfall.

50
00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:59.211
Anne decides to test how waterproof her jacket is and steps underneath the falls.

51
00:03:59.231 --> 00:04:02.093
"It felt like a massage!"

52
00:04:02.654 --> 00:04:06.136
she says, emerging from the waterfall dry and smiling.

53
00:04:07.337 --> 00:04:12.061
The four days of hiking go by faster than they expected, and soon Josh and Anne are at

54
00:04:12.101 --> 00:04:12.981
the end of the trail.

55
00:04:13.001 --> 00:04:15.823
"What did you think of Milford?"

56
00:04:16.384 --> 00:04:16.884
Anne asked.

57
00:04:16.904 --> 00:04:20.547
"It's so beautiful, my feet aren't even tired!"

58
00:04:21.187 --> 00:04:21.828
said Josh.

59
00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:23.349
"I agree.

60
00:04:23.769 --> 00:04:26.090
I can't wait to come back and do it again!"

61
00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:27.111
said Anne.

62
00:04:27.651 --> 00:04:29.092
The first trail was a success.

63
00:04:29.872 --> 00:04:35.115
With another 12 days to go, Josh and Anne are thankful they have such great gear and such

64
00:04:35.155 --> 00:04:36.476
a beautiful country to visit.
